{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The agent asks only for outgoing edges and submits without reading\n contents. Its renderer is required by the agent interface, but any\n rendering would imply an unwanted content input. Other agent tests\n exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation is on an explicit function with a body, `render` in `impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]`. Its commentary is in a fenced citation block, as the built-in requires. The explanation is substantive and matches the current source.\n\n- **Renderer is never reached.** The test script in `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` issues only `outgoing_edges` and `submit_result`. In `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs`, `Conversation::dispatch` calls `renderer.render` only in the `read_node` branch.\n- **Direct ask does not render.** The criterion calls `ctx.ask::<bool>()` with no insertions. `Ask::execute` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs` renders only for nodes produced by insertions, so there is none here.\n- **Renderer is required.** `AgentInputRenderer::render` is a required trait method, so the type must implement it. A real rendering would imply a content read the test is designed to forbid. The panic body acts as a guard.\n- **Other tests cover rendering.** `Renderer` and `DistinctPages` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` render real contents. Tests such as `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` and `retries_and_cut_off_tools_preserve_inputs_and_submission_skips_other_reads` request `read_node`. This supports the claim about other agent tests.\n\nThe citation is a built-in coverage exception, not a project requirement. It is not redundant with any `{impl}` or `{test}` reference on the item, so I found no gap.",
